return [====[EGEND OF DEBORAH · 67</div></article><article class="page" id="fund" data-title="The Debbie Fund"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>The Debbie Fund</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Deborah demonstrates" class="art" style="background-size:300% 200%;background-position:0% 0%"></div><p>The Debbie Fund takes rescue funding very seriously. Its $DEB units are Debbie Coins—&#x27;Debs&#x27;—and its collectibles are Debbie Fund Tokens, or DFTs. These are server-local game records, with no cash value or outside wallet.</p><p>A successful rescue creates a pool of 100 × Dungeon Level Debs. Qualifying Soldier-attributable Hero life losses assign 11% each to the Soldier side, capped at 33% of the pool; Soldier damage contributions determine its allocation.</p><p>The remaining Hero pool is divided half equally and half by damage and effective allied healing, with hostile-loss adjustments. Eligible dead or disconnected participants can retain their claim. Switching to Soldier play forfeits a Hero share.</p><p>Rescue awards increase wallet balance and lifetime rescue earnings. DFT sales increase spendable balance but do not inflate that lifetime rescue score. The staging Heroes of Legend board records the highest dungeon reached, damsels rescued, and cash bags recovered; it is not a count of monster kills.</p><p>At Debbie, choose Fuse Equipment, Sell Equipment, Fuse DFTs, or Sell DFTs. Drag eligible items into the labeled pile, review the value, and confirm. You can also click items to add or remove them. Closing the menu cancels staging without moving anything. Sales award the displayed value in $DEB. Fusion consumes two to eight inputs and returns one legal item worth 85–100% of their combined value and more than any single input; unsupported piles are rejected intact. Equipment fusion returns carried gear; DFT fusion returns a persistent upgraded token. DFT-created gear and free starting weapons cannot be sold or fused. If any fused DFT was recreated this run, the new token remains used for this run. DFT Collection / Recreate retains the free recreation service.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 68</div></article><article class="page" id="tokens" data-title="A little something to keep"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>A little something to keep</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Deborah demonstrates" class="art" style="background-size:300% 200%;background-position:100% 0%"></div><p>DFTs normally mint when a dungeon objective is completed. Combat Level milestones 1, 5, 10, and 20 can each award one token per account on this server. A rare rescue roll also gives each participating Hero a one-in-1,000 chance. Ordinary enemy kills do not mint DFTs. The treasure chest event can also award DFTs; see Treasure to keep. Rescuing Deborah at Level 20 also unlocks Abundance: visit her in staging for one free DFT per Steam account every rolling 24 hours. Reconnecting or restarting a campaign does not reset the timer. The eight-token capacity still applies; a full wallet leaves the gift available until you make room. Recreated equipment retains the usual resale and fusion exclusions.</p><p>Your collection has eight slots. Milestone items waiting for space stay frozen; making room does not reroll them. Tokens persist across ordinary death and campaign restart.</p><p>At the staging Debbie statue, recreate a token&#x27;s frozen item for free once per token per run. The DFT remains in your collection. The same token becomes available to recreate again in the next run.</p><p>You may instead sell a DFT permanently for its displayed Value in Debs. Read the confirmation carefully: selling the token removes it. Wallet viewing is portable; the statue&#x27;s staging, proximity, and role rules still govern its physical services.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 69</div></article><article class="page" id="dungeon-events" data-title="Dungeon Events: discoveries and obstacles"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Dungeon Events: discoveries and obstacles</h2><table><tr><td>Slot machine · $5 DEB stake</td><td>One ordinary d4: 4 pays $15 gross (+$10 net); 1–3 pays nothing (−$5 net).</td></tr><tr><td>Odds</td><td>25% win; 75% loss. No exploding dice or ability bonuses.</td></tr></table><p>An enabled dungeon contains 1–4 different event types, chosen by one ordinary, non-exploding d4. A result of 1–3 selects that many from Debbie Slots, locked loot chests, vending machines, False-floor hazards, bribe blockades, Skeleton of a Hero blockades, and the Game Master’s Equipment Quiz; warp holes join this common pool from Dungeon Level 5 onward. A 4 selects three common types plus a DFT treasure event. Treasure therefore appears on 25% of event selections; its one or two physical chests count as one event type. A paired warp hole also counts once. Events never replace the required rescue objective.</p><p>Debbie Slots is optional and never blocks the rescue route. Read its posted stake and odds before pressing E to play. Each Steam account may complete one play per dungeon; reconnecting or beginning a replacement Hero does not grant another play. Other Heroes have their own attempt.</p><p>The stake uses your persistent, server-local $DEB balance, which has no cash value. A completed play applies the stake and payout together. Insufficient funds or a storage failure spends nothing and leaves your attempt available; retrying does not reroll the outcome. Leaving the dungeon ends access to that machine.</p><p>Events are enabled by default on new server configurations. Servers retaining an earlier disabled setting need an administrator to set lod_events_enabled 1 for future dungeon generation.</p><p>In developer mode, administrators can run lod_event_population_preview to generate a normal 1–4 event selection and print its locations, or lod_event_preview_generate followed by an event name for a single-event preview. Previews mark the campaign unranked but still use carried keys and persistent server-local funds and DFTs; they provide no free currency. Regenerating the same dungeon does not refresh account claims.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 70</div></article><article class="page" id="locked-chest" data-title="A key, or a Rogue’s touch"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>A key, or a Rogue’s touch</h2><table><tr><td>Chest Key</td><td>Bag-only consumable; stacks up to nine. Press E at a locked chest to use one.</td></tr><tr><td>Rogue lockpick</td><td>Press E without a key, or hold Sprint + E to pick while carrying keys.</td></tr><tr><td>Success chance</td><td>5% per Combat Level, up to 95%; one ordinary d100 roll.</td></tr></table><p>The locked loot chest sits off the required rescue route and offers each Steam account one ordinary procedural wearable per dungeon. It does not award a DFT; the item uses your normal equipment storage.</p><p>Chest Keys can appear among normal loot drops and remain in your bag rather than the Throwable slot. A key is spent only when its chest item successfully enters your equipment storage. A full bag or failed delivery spends no key; make room or retry.</p><p>A Rogue gets one lockpick attempt per chest. Failure uses that attempt but leaves any key intact, and you may later open the chest with a key. A full bag or another rejected preflight does not use the attempt. If a successful pick cannot deliver the item, retry to claim the same reward without another roll or a key.</p><p>The chest remembers your account’s claim and lockpick attempt through reconnects, replacement Heroes, and regeneration of the same dungeon. Those actions cannot grant another attempt or reroll the reward. A new dungeon provides a new opportunity; a new campaign resets the chest record.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 71</div></article><article class="page" id="treasure-chest" data-title="Treasure to keep"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Treasure to keep</h2><table><tr><td>DFT treasure event</td><td>One ordinary d2 selects one or two optional chests; each chest offers each Steam account one DFT.</td></tr><tr><td>Collection capacity</td><td>Eight DFTs. Ordinary equipment bag space does not limit this reward.</td></tr><tr><td>Opening the lock</td><td>Use a Chest Key, or use the same Rogue lockpicking controls and chance as an ordinary locked chest.</td></tr></table><p>Treasure chests hold persistent Debbie Fund Tokens, not ordinary equipment pickups. Each Hero has an independent claim at each chest. The reward is fixed: reconnecting, replacing your Hero, or regenerating the same dungeon cannot reroll it or restore a claim. Selling or recreating the awarded DFT does not reopen the chest.</p><p>Press E to spend one Chest Key when the DFT is successfully delivered. A Rogue without a key may pick the lock; hold Sprint + E to choose lockpicking while carrying keys. Each account gets one attempt per chest at 5% per Combat Level, up to 95%. A failed pick consumes the attempt but no key; you can return with a key.</p><p>A full DFT collection spends neither key nor lockpick attempt. Make room in your collection, then return. A storage failure spends no key. If a successful pick cannot deliver its DFT, the chest stays unlocked for your account: retry for the same reward without another roll or key.</p><p>Treasure events appear only on a four-event selection and contain one or two optional chests. Their DFTs persist in your server-local collection and have no cash value. Leaving the dungeon ends access to its chests. For an administrator preview, use lod_event_preview_generate treasure_chest; lod_chest_key_testkit supplies one key only if you have none.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 72</div></article><article class="page" id="vending-machine" data-title="A bottle for the road"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>A bottle for the road</h2><table><tr><td>Healing Potion · $10 DEB</td><td>One bottle per Steam account per campaign dungeon. Each Hero has an independent purchase.</td></tr><tr><td>Potion effect</td><td>Restores 25 HP and cures negative statuses when used. Buying the bottle does not heal you.</td></tr><tr><td>Carrying capacity</td><td>Healing Potions stack up to three and use the Throwable slot.</td></tr></table><p>Press E at a vending machine to buy one standard Healing Potion for your equipment inventory. The price uses your persistent, server-local $DEB balance, which has no cash value. The potion is ordinary run equipment, not a DFT.</p><p>Insufficient funds, a full potion stack, a storage failure, or leaving the interaction before it can complete spends nothing and leaves your purchase available. Correct the problem and retry. A successful purchase charges exactly $10 DEB and delivers one bottle.</p><p>The machine remembers your account’s completed purchase through death, replacement Heroes, reconnects, and regeneration of the same dungeon. Drinking or discarding the bottle does not restock the machine, and reconnecting does not replace a lost bottle. A new dungeon or campaign provides a new purchase.</p><p>This optional machine can appear alongside other Dungeon Events. For an administrator preview, use lod_event_preview_generate vending_machine. Purchases spend real server-local $DEB; the preview does not provide free currency.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 73</div></article><article class="page" id="false-floor" data-title="Watch your step"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Watch your step</h2><p>A False-floor hazard is a small panel in an optional upper-floor room. Stepping fully onto it as a grounded Hero can open the floor beneath you. There is no E prompt to activate it. The solid rim around the panel gives you room to go around.</p><p>The fall leads one floor down. Ordinary gravity and falling consequences apply. The destination preserves your current progression access, and the existing stairs provide a route back; the trap never opens a locked progression shortcut.</p><p>The panel stays open for at least three seconds. It closes and rearms only after its opening is clear, so keep moving after landing. All Heroes share the same panel state, and the hazard can trigger again. If the landing is unsafe or occupied before activation, the panel stays closed.</p><p>For an administrator preview, use lod_event_preview_generate false_floor. Redeploy after generation and follow the printed locator.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 74</div></article><article class="page" id="warp-hole" data-title="A shorter way back"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>A shorter way back</h2><p>From Dungeon Level 5 onward, a paired warp hole may appear as an optional event. Its two cyan endpoints sit on different physical floors. The prompt identifies your endpoint and its destination floor.</p><p>Press E at either dormant endpoint. Your first successful traversal links the pair for everyone until this dungeon ends. Linked holes are free and repeatable; wait one second between your own traversals. Other Heroes can use them independently.</p><p>A warp hole shortens a route you can already reach. It never skips a locked gate, required boss, key or rescue step, and the ordinary stairs still provide a way back. It preserves your facing and stops your previous momentum.</p><p>If the arrival is occupied or unsafe, you stay where you are. Clear the landing and try again. A refused first traversal leaves the pair dormant. Regeneration replaces both endpoints with a fresh dormant pair.</p><p>For an administrator preview, use lod_event_preview_generate warp_hole. This unranked single-event preview can show the pair before Dungeon Level 5. Redeploy after generation and follow the printed locators.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 75</div></article><article class="page" id="bribe-blockade" data-title="Pay the toll — or find the collateral"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Pay the toll — or find the collateral</h2><p>A bribe blockade closes a required route until one Hero surrenders at least 50 $DEB of equipment value. It opens for the whole party. No cash leaves your wallet; excess item value is not returned as change.</p><p>You always have a route to a lost-property cache on the approachable side. Press E at the cache to earmark its generated ring as shared collateral. The ring stays safely in the cache until payment: it cannot be worn, sold, discarded or lost. Finding it never consumes your equipment.</p><p>Press E at the toll terminal to review payment. Choose the recovered ring, or select 1–8 of your own unequipped procedural wearables worth at least 50 in total. Weapons, consumables, protected or free starting gear and DFT-created equipment are excluded. Heroes do not pool partial payments.</p><p>Read the item names and total, then confirm. Cancel or close the review to spend nothing. Reviews expire after 45 seconds; moving away or changing your inventory, Hero or life invalidates payment. Use the terminal again to retry. Another Hero’s completed payment opens the barrier without charging you.</p><p>The passage stays open until this dungeon generation ends. Late arrivals see the same open state. Regeneration replaces the toll and collateral; completed payments are not refunded. The blockade never bypasses the normal keycard, boss or rescue sequence.</p><p>Administrator preview: lod_event_preview_generate bribe_blockade. Redeploy and follow the printed terminal and cache locators. The preview is unranked and any confirmed payment uses the actual selected equipment.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 76</div></article><article class="page" id="tips" data-title="Deborah&#x27;s parting advice"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Deborah&#x27;s parting advice</h2><div role="img" aria-label="Deborah demonstrates" class="art" style="background-size:300% 200%;background-position:50% 100%"></div><ol><li>The clock pauses in staging and starts when the first Hero deploys. Every new dungeon gives you thirty minutes.</li><li>Keep a useful spell selected. A bottle in your hand means you are holding a bottle—not casting.</li><li>Move sideways out of committed charges. A longer corridor is not always a safer escape.</li><li>Compare gear drawbacks as carefully as benefits. Keep your permanent feat requirements in mind.</li><li>Use short map checks, read the current objective, and remember the stairs.</li><li>When the Warden falls, finish the job. At Level 20, defeat Hector too. Then Jail Key, jail door, rescue target.</li></ol><blockquote>“You&#x27;ve read the book. Now make yourself useful.”<br>— Deborah</blockquote><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 77</div></article><article class="page" id="skeleton-blockade" data-title="Skeleton of a Hero"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>Skeleton of a Hero</h2><table><tr><td>Class</td><td>Fighter, Rogue or Wizard, chosen when the dungeon is built.</td></tr><tr><td>Combat Level</td><td>Dungeon Level + 2, capped at 20.</td></tr><tr><td>Passage</td><td>Defeat the Skeleton once; the route opens for everyone.</td></tr></table><p>A Skeleton of a Hero guards a required passage. Its name begins “Skeleton of” and comes from the same name generator as your Hero. Its abilities, identity perks, class growth, health dice and eligible automatic feats use the ordinary Hero framework, with AI choices restricted to abilities its controller can use.</p><p>The Fighter closes in for melee, the Rogue fires SMG bursts, and the Wizard warns before striking a ground arc. Wizard arcs spend 12 base Magic plus their Content cost, modified by ordinary offensive Magic rules. Wizards cycle their generated Contents and must regenerate when their Magic runs low. Shared defenses, status effects and class rules still apply.</p><p>The Skeleton is always on the approachable side of its barrier. Fight it before crossing. A legitimate defeat opens the tall barrier for every Hero, including later arrivals; your normal keycard, boss and rescue sequence remains intact. Regenerating the dungeon creates a fresh encounter.</p><p>Combat XP follows ordinary killing-blow and damage-contribution rules, and normal individualized enemy drops apply. There is no extra cash, DFT or guaranteed equipment award. Removing the enemy is not a combat victory.</p><p>Administrator preview: lod_event_preview_generate skeleton_blockade. Redeploy and follow the printed location. The preview is unranked.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 78</div></article><article class="page" id="equipment-quiz" data-title="The Game Master: know what you wear"><div class="kicker">How to play</div><h2>The Game Master: know what you wear</h2><table><tr><td>Before accepting</td><td>One attempt per account per dungeon. Decline freely.</td></tr><tr><td>Correct answer</td><td>One DFT, only when collection succeeds.</td></tr><tr><td>Wrong answer</td><td>The real worn item is stolen.</td></tr><tr><td>Time limit</td><td>30 seconds after acceptance; the dungeon keeps running.</td></tr></table><p>A suspiciously familiar grin waits in an optional hidden alcove. Press E at the Game Master and read his offer. You have 30 seconds to accept. Your task is to identify one piece of equipment you are wearing among two plausible phonies. The three cards show names, slots and properties. You cannot consult Equipment, Character Sheet, Wallet or the other Player Menu pages while answering.</p><p>Only ordinary procedural wearables are at risk. Weapons, consumables, protected or bound gear, free starting items and DFT-created equipment are excluded. Paired gloves count as one item and occupy both hands. No eligible equipment, a full eight-token DFT collection or unavailable reward storage means no accepted attempt.</p><p>Answer within 30 seconds. A wrong submitted answer removes the selected real item and its equipment effects. Cancelling, closing, timing out, dying, disconnecting, moving out of range or line of sight, or losing the current challenge forfeits the attempt without theft or reward. The world does not pause or protect you.</p><p>A correct answer earns one persistent, server-local DFT with no cash value. If storage fails after your answer, the result reads pending rather than success. Your menus reopen; use the same Game Master to retry the same frozen reward while the same Hero life, worn item and dungeon remain valid. Losing that binding forfeits an uncollected reward.</p><p>The Game Master disappears for you after your attempt ends. Other Heroes retain their own independent attempt and may play simultaneously. Reconnecting, changing Heroes or regenerating this dungeon does not grant another attempt. A new dungeon does. Late arrivals see the encounter appropriate to their own account.</p><p>Administrator preview: lod_event_preview_generate equipment_quiz. Redeploy with eligible ordinary wearable equipment and follow the printed locator. The preview is unranked but confirmed play risks actual equipment and awards a persistent DFT.</p><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 79</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_academic_achievement" data-title="Academic Achievement"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Academic Achievement</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_ACADEMIC_ACHIEVEMENT"><h3>Academic Achievement</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / magic_pool</p><p>Add your positive CHA modifier to your INT modifier when calculating passive Magic regeneration. Regeneration must be permitted.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 80</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_aggressive_personality" data-title="Aggressive Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Aggressive Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_AGGRESSIVE_PERSONALITY"><h3>Aggressive Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / eligible physical attack</p><p>Your next physical attack adds your positive CHA modifier as damage to each target. Cooldown: 1d3 seconds; these timing dice do not explode.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 81</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_aura_burst" data-title="Aura Burst"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Aura Burst</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_AURA_BURST_1"><h3>Aura Burst</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage to enemies within 0 same-floor cells. Sustained drain does not trigger this.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_RADIANCE_2"><h3>Radiance</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Aura Burst</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage to enemies within 1 same-floor cells. Sustained drain does not trigger this. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MAJESTY_3"><h3>Majesty</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Radiance</p><p>When you successfully spend Magic on a discrete action, deal your positive CHA modifier as extra Magic damage to enemies within 2 same-floor cells. Sustained drain does not trigger this. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 82</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_hitstun_presence" data-title="Unnerving Presence"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Unnerving Presence</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_1"><h3>Unnerving Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 10% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_2"><h3>Dazing Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Unnerving Presence</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 20% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_3"><h3>Overwhelming Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dazing Presence</p><p>Increase hit stun you inflict by 30% after CHA scaling. Resistance, retrigger protection and duration caps still apply. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 83</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_intimidation_proc" data-title="Daunting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Daunting</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_1"><h3>Daunting</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 11% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_2"><h3>Cowing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Daunting</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 22% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_3"><h3>Overawing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Cowing</p><p>Your damaging hit has a 33% chance to force a surviving target to check Morale. Requires its Morale cooldown to be ready; skips hits that already force a check. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 84</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_menace" data-title="Menacing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Menacing</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_1"><h3>Menacing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Gain +2 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 30% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_2"><h3>Dreadful</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Menacing</p><p>Gain +4 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 25% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_3"><h3>Terrifying</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>Gain +4 Morale DC. A hit exceeding 20% of a human target’s MaxHP can trigger Morale; low HP alone cannot. Each target’s first Morale save against you per encounter rolls twice and keeps the lower die. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 85</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_nerve" data-title="Iron Nerve"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Iron Nerve</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_NERVE_1"><h3>Iron Nerve</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Gain +2 to Morale saves.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors subject to Morale</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_NERVE_2"><h3>Unbreakable Nerve</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Iron Nerve</p><p>Gain +4 to Morale saves. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors subject to Morale</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 86</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_panic" data-title="Panic Is Contagious"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Panic Is Contagious</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_PANIC"><h3>Panic Is Contagious</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>When an enemy fails Morale against you, AI enemies below half HP within 2 connected cells make a Morale check. This cannot cascade again; each target is immune to cascades for 3 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 87</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_personality_aura" data-title="Abrasive Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Abrasive Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_ABRASIVE_PERSONALITY_1"><h3>Abrasive Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Every 3d4 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage to enemies within 0 same-floor cells. Timing dice do not explode.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_NARCISSISM_2"><h3>Narcissism</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Abrasive Personality</p><p>Every 3d4 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage to enemies within 1 same-floor cells. Timing dice do not explode. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MEGALOMANIA_3"><h3>Megalomania</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Narcissism</p><p>Every 3d4 seconds, deal your positive CHA modifier as untyped damage to enemies within 2 same-floor cells. Timing dice do not explode. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 88</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_self_actualization" data-title="Self-Actualization"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Self-Actualization</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_SELF_ACTUALIZATION"><h3>Self-Actualization</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / eligible Magic Form</p><p>Add your positive CHA modifier to each target’s magical damage, once after damage multipliers.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 89</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_winning_personality" data-title="Winning Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Winning Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_WINNING_PERSONALITY"><h3>Winning Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17</p><p>Gain +1 intrinsic CHA, up to the ability ceiling. Use the higher of INT or CHA to meet INT feat ability requirements. Other prerequisites still apply.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 90</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_big_guy" data-title="Big Guy"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Big Guy</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BIG_GUY"><h3>Big Guy</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 and STR 13</p><p>Your body and hurt volume become 30% larger. Gain 15% melee reach and 20% physical push dealt. Your movement hull stays the same. Incompatible with Little Guy.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 91</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_blast_proof" data-title="Blast-Proof"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Blast-Proof</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BLAST_PROOF"><h3>Blast-Proof</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Stop the first continuation of an incoming exploding damage chain. Keep damage already rolled; other chains continue normally. Cooldown: 2 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 92</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_glow_up" data-title="Glow Up"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Glow Up</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_GLOW_UP"><h3>Glow Up</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires a usable explicit CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p><p>Whenever your own ability adds your positive CHA modifier as damage, also add your positive CON modifier once to that damage event.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an authored CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 93</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_health_regeneration" data-title="Second Wind"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Second Wind</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_11"><h3>Second Wind</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 11% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_22"><h3>Rapid Recovery</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Second Wind</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 22% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_33"><h3>Unbroken</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Rapid Recovery</p><p>After 5 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1% MaxHP per second, scaled by CON. Add 33% MaxHP to your regeneration ceiling; this stacks with Fighter’s innate 33% and cannot restore Tetris overfill. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 94</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_not_yet" data-title="Not Yet"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Not Yet</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_NOT_YET"><h3>Not Yet</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Once per dungeon, lethal damage received above 1 HP leaves you at 1 HP and grants 0.5 seconds of damage immunity. Death, respawn and reconnect do not restore this use.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 95</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_poison_proc" data-title="Venomous"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Venomous</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_1"><h3>Venomous</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Your hit has a 11% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_2"><h3>Toxic</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Venomous</p><p>Your hit has a 22% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_3"><h3>Virulent</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Toxic</p><p>Your hit has a 33% chance to attempt Poisoned. The target saves with CON against your CON modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 96</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_steadfast" data-title="Hard to Move"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hard to Move</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_STEADFAST"><h3>Hard to Move</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Reduce ordinary hit-stun duration and incoming push distance by 25%. Scripted boss effects may ignore this resistance.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 97</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_big_scary" data-title="Big Scary"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Big Scary</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_BIG_SCARY"><h3>Big Scary</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15, STR 13, and CHA 15 / Big Guy; Menacing</p><p>Gain +2 Morale DC when dealing melee damage, physical push or wall-crush damage. This stacks with Menacing.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 98</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_boom_battery" data-title="Boom Battery"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Boom Battery</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_BOOM_BATTERY"><h3>Boom Battery</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 and INT 15 / Capability: exploding_nonmagic_damage_dice</p><p>Every second continuation die in a non-Magic attack restores 1 Magic. Maximum: 5 Magic per attack; never above 100 Magic.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 99</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_crush_panic" data-title="Crash the Party"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Crash the Party</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_CRUSH_PANIC"><h3>Crash the Party</h3><p class="requirement">STR 17 and CHA 17 / Pusher; Dreadful</p><p>Your wall crush forces an eligible target to check Morale, even during its normal recheck cooldown. Once per target every 3 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with physical push</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 100</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_force_of_will" data-title="Force of Will"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Force of Will</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_FORCE_OF_WILL"><h3>Force of Will</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 and WIS 15 / Pusher; Force Multiplier</p><p>Magic that already pushes can trigger Pusher, Shover or Space Hog after Force Multiplier. A successful proc adds 168 units and uses your Pusher wall-slam die. Shared per-target cooldown: 0.5 seconds.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, eligible AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 101</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_meteor_strike" data-title="Meteor Strike"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Meteor Strike</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_METEOR_STRIKE"><h3>Meteor Strike</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 and INT 15 / Bash; Cloud Step</p><p>After using Cloud Step, your first Crowbar hit before landing adds one exploding d6 and doubles its Crowbar push. A miss does not consume this strike. Landing resets it.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers with Crowbar-family access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 102</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_tiny_terror" data-title="Tiny Terror"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Tiny Terror</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_TINY_TERROR"><h3>Tiny Terror</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 and CHA 15 / Little Guy; Menacing</p><p>While Little Guy is active, gain +2 Morale DC against enemies within 2 connected cells. This stacks with Menacing.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 103</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_burst_size" data-title="Extra Round"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Extra Round</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_1"><h3>Extra Round</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Add 1 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_2"><h3>Extended Volley</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Extra Round</p><p>Add 2 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_3"><h3>Full Barrage</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Extended Volley</p><p>Add 3 rounds to existing multi-shot bursts at their normal spacing and damage, with no extra ammunition cost. Single shots and Shotgun pellets are not bursts. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 104</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_clumsy_proc" data-title="Distracting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Distracting</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_1"><h3>Distracting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your hit has a 11% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_2"><h3>Disorienting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Distracting</p><p>Your hit has a 22% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_3"><h3>Discombobulating</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Disorienting</p><p>Your hit has a 33% chance to attempt Clumsy. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 105</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_exploding_damage_dice" data-title="Perfect Ten"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Perfect Ten</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D10"><h3>Perfect Ten</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your ordinary d10 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 10 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d10 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D8"><h3>Eight Is Enough</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Perfect Ten</p><p>Your ordinary d8 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 8 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d8 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D4"><h3>Fourtunate</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Eight Is Enough</p><p>Your ordinary d4 damage dice explode on their maximum face. Continuations explode at 4 minus BoomShift, minimum 2. Maximum: 32 dice per chain. Earlier die unlocks remain active.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d4 damage rolls</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 106</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_immolate_proc" data-title="Singeing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Singeing</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_1"><h3>Singeing</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Your hit has a 11% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_2"><h3>Scorching</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Singeing</p><p>Your hit has a 22% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_3"><h3>Incendiary</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Scorching</p><p>Your hit has a 33% chance to attempt Immolated. The target saves with DEX against your DEX modifier; success prevents the condition. Hits already attempting that condition do not roll again. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 107</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_magnum_deadeye" data-title="Deadeye"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Deadeye</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_MAGNUM_DEADEYE"><h3>Deadeye</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Stand perfectly still for 0.5 seconds to empower your next primary attack: double damage with a standard weapon, or triple damage with the .357 Magnum. One attack consumes the aim.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled actors using a standard player weapon</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 108</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_rate_of_fire" data-title="Hair Trigger"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hair Trigger</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_1"><h3>Hair Trigger</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Increase ordinary firearm primary-fire rate by 10%. Reloads, cooling, targeting windups and spacing within bursts stay unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_2"><h3>Rapid Fire</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Hair Trigger</p><p>Increase ordinary firearm primary-fire rate by 20%. Reloads, cooling, targeting windups and spacing within bursts stay unchanged. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_3"><h3>Lead Storm</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Rapid Fire</p><p>Increase ordinary firearm primary-fire rate by 30%. Reloads, cooling, targeting windups and spacing within bursts stay unchanged. Replaces lower ranks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 109</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_reload_cadence" data-title="Quick Reload"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Quick Reload</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD"><h3>Quick Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Reduce ordinary weapon reload time by 20%. This does not shorten SMG cooling or attack windups.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p>]====]
